  <title>Object navigation</title>
  <p>
    Object navigation lets you move through the accessible object hierarchy without moving
    application focus or the caret. It is not limited to objects visible on screen.
  </p>
  <p>
    Applications provide objects in a hierarchy: a parent contains child objects, and children
    with the same parent are siblings. For example, a toolbar can contain several buttons.
    Object navigation uses a separate navigator focus; the commands below explore and interact
    with the object at that location.
  </p>
  <section id="commands-object-navigation">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Object navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Click on the object with navigator focus.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Enter</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
        <p>
          Acts on the object with navigator focus. Orca first tries suitable accessible actions
          exposed by the object through its application or toolkit. If no suitable action
          succeeds, Orca tries to simulate a mouse click at the object's location. This fallback
          does not currently work on Wayland. Accessible actions can still work on Wayland when
          supported by the application or toolkit.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Go to the first child of the object with navigator focus.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Down Arrow</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Go to the next sibling of the object with navigator focus.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Right Arrow</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Go to the parent of the object with navigator focus.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Up Arrow</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Go to the previous sibling of the object with navigator focus.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>Left Arrow</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle simplified object navigation.</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>Ctrl</key>
            <key>S</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
        <p>
          Turns simplified object navigation on or off. Simplified navigation hides some
          layout-only objects to make the hierarchy easier to explore.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
